text:
{
  "opening": "This release introduces significant enhancements to grammar reconstruction, forest transformation capabilities, and standalone tooling. It also ensures robust handling of ambiguous intermediates and improves error reporting reliability through data structure adjustments.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "The public API must expose the function `isascii` as a top-level name. This function should correctly identify whether a given string contains only ASCII characters."
    },
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The library must provide improved performance and accuracy for parsing tree reconstruction via the `Reconstructor` class. New utility functions `make_recons_rule` and `make_recons_rule_to_term` must be available to facilitate custom reconstruction logic."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28",
      "text": "The parser must continue to support LALR(1) analysis using `LALR_Analyzer` and handle unexpected input gracefully with `UnexpectedInput`. The utility function `isascii` must remain accessible at the module level."
    },
    {
      "id": "m37",
      "text": "The parser must correctly expand ambiguous intermediate nodes during parsing using `AmbiguousIntermediateExpander`. Visitors such as `ForestToAmbiguousTreeVisitor` and `CompleteForestToAmbiguousTreeVisitor` must be available to traverse and transform packed parse trees."
    },
    {
      "id": "m51",
      "text": "Grammar error reports must consistently display terminal and non-terminal information in a deterministic order. This ensures that repeated parsing attempts yield identical error messages regardless of internal dictionary ordering."
    },
    {
      "id": "m52",
      "text": "The `Token` and `Tree` classes must support evaluable representations suitable for debugging or serialization. The function `pydot__tree_to_graph` must be exposed to convert parse trees into graphviz dot format."
    },
    {
      "id": "m54",
      "text": "The library must expose the `TreeForestTransformer` class and the `handles_ambiguity` attribute on transformer instances. These components enable unified transformation of both single trees and packed forests while preserving ambiguity information."
    },
    {
      "id": "m59",
      "text": "The `main` function in `lark.tools.standalone` must accept a `print` parameter to control output destination. The `strip_docstrings` function must remain available for preprocessing grammar files before standalone generation."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please verify that all listed public names are correctly exported and that the new behaviors align with the documented expectations. Ensure backward compatibility is maintained for existing users relying on the core parsing and transformation APIs."
}
